DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 6

GitLab & GitLab CI/CD Basics (0–2 Years Experience)

GitLab is more than a code repository.
It’s a complete DevOps platform used by many organizations for source control, CI/CD, and automation.

Interviewers often expect freshers to understand how GitLab pipelines actually work.

📌 Tool 6 Focus: GitLab & CI/CD Interview Questions

• What is GitLab and how is it different from GitHub?
• What is GitLab CI/CD?
• What is a pipeline in GitLab?
• Where do you define GitLab CI configuration?
• What is .gitlab-ci.yml?
• Explain stages, jobs, and pipelines
• What is a GitLab runner?
• Difference between shared runner and specific runner
• What is an executor in GitLab runner?
• What are artifacts in GitLab CI?
• Difference between artifacts and cache
• What are variables in GitLab CI?
• How do you store secrets securely in GitLab?
• What are environments in GitLab CI/CD?
• What is a manual job?
• What are approvals in GitLab pipelines?
• How do you trigger pipelines automatically?
• How do you run pipelines for merge
requests?
• How do you deploy to different environments using GitLab?
• Common GitLab CI mistakes beginners make
• Real-world GitLab CI/CD use case

💡 Interview Tip:
If you explain a simple flow like:
 Commit → Pipeline → Build → Test → Deploy
interviewers know you understand CI/CD practically, not just theoretically.
